      "message": "feat(sinker): read a welded wall face as its vertical strips\n\nA rounded-corner pocket's wall band welds into one smooth face\n(FeatureSel::Patch). The electrode-from-faces read refused that pick\nas \"a curved wall\". Now the app expands the patch into its planar\nstrips, and the new motion rule sinker_cavity::welded_wall holds each\nstrip to the vertical-wall rule. The cavity read then stands each strip\non the floor ring like any wall. The floor and the welded face give the\nsame body electrode as the planar-strip pick (#1152), and its burn is\njudged clean. A strip that leans or is level refuses the welded face by\nname.\n\nSynthetic conditions only. Not exercised on a real EDM control.\n\nFixes #1808\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
